# Domain Glossary

## Tournament types (spec §1, §1.1)

- **ACC (Atmiya Cricket Club)** — Leather Ball. Four fixed teams (ACC 3, ACC 6, ACC 9, ACC 0) that collectively play the external BEDCL league. 25 overs, max 5 overs/bowler, 16 matches/team/season.
- **APL (Atmiya Premier League)** — Tennis Ball. All cities of the province participate. Organized by Club Manager.
- **Center-level** — Tennis Ball. One or multiple cities, but **not all** (all cities ⇒ it's APL). Organized by Center Sevak or Club Manager.

### Type-resolution logic (on tournament creation, §1.1)

1. Ball Type = **Leather** → **ACC** rules.
2. Ball Type = **Tennis** AND creator is **Club Manager** AND city option is **ALL** → **APL** rules.
3. Ball Type = **Tennis** AND (creator is **Center Sevak**) OR (creator is **Club Manager** with single/multi but not all cities) → **Center-level** rules.

## Roles (spec §2)

Eight first-class roles, plus the Scorer per-match grant and the unauthenticated Guest:

- **Admin** — platform-wide; acts on any tournament, edits any scorecard, views the full audit log.
- **Club Manager** — organizes ACC and APL; manages fees; reshuffles ACC teams; can edit ACC scorecards post-confirmation.
- **Center Sevak** — organizes Center-level; approves registrations for their Center; updates ratings/availability for own-Center players in APL.
- **Captain** — per-team; selects Playing 11 (ACC), assigns per-match Scorer (ACC), handles suspension overrides, confirms scorecards.
- **Vice Captain** — inherits Captain permissions while Captain is suspended; can confirm scorecards and perform scoring.
- **Manager** — **APL and Center-level ONLY.** Shares favouriting/player-add permissions with Captain/VC.
- **Player** — registers, votes in availability polls, views own stats, edits own profile.
- **Scorer (per-match grant)** — a permission granted to a Player for one specific match; auto-revoked at match completion. **Not a top-level role.**
- **Guest** — read-only, no auth: live match, scorecards, leaderboards, YouTube embed.
- *(System is an internal audit-attribution actor only — not a login-capable role.)*

## Critical rule

**Manager does NOT exist in ACC.** ACC teams have no Manager. Hide the Manager
option from any Captain/Vice Captain/Manager UI when the tournament type is ACC
(RBAC footnote D1).
